course: dictionary
lesson: 58
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. «She drew the ace of hearts from the pack.» Here ace is a playing card, because the pack and hearts are clues.
explain: «Mo is an ace at football, and he scored three goals.» Mo is not a playing card. An ace here is a person who is very good at something, so the words around it show the meaning.
explain: «Priya aced her spelling test, getting every word right.» To ace something means to do it perfectly. Check by swapping in your meaning: "Priya did her spelling test perfectly" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: In tennis, an ace is a serve the other player cannot touch. In casual talk, ace means excellent: «That was ace!» When you meet a word with many meanings, ask which one fits the clues.
fact: Ace can be a noun, an adjective or a verb, so it has several meanings.
fact: An ace is a playing card with one mark on it.
fact: «To ace a test» means to do it perfectly.
fact: «An ace up your sleeve» means a secret advantage that you save until you need it.
fact: In informal talk, «ace» means excellent or great, and «ace» can also mean doing really well at something.
exercise: «She drew the ace of spades from the pack.» What is an ace here? | *A playing card | A secret trick | A tennis serve | A very good player
exercise: «Mo is an ace at football.» What does ace mean here? | *A very skilled person | A loud shout | A kind of football | A short, sharp word
exercise: «Priya aced her spelling test.» What does aced mean? | *Did it perfectly | Took it again later | Lost her pencil | Shouted the answers
test: «In tennis, Sam served an ace, and his opponent could not touch the ball.» What is an ace in tennis? | *A serve the other player cannot touch | A long, slow rally | A kind of tennis racket | A point lost by mistake
test: Maya says, «That film was ace!» What does ace mean? | *Excellent | Very wet | Very small | Boring
exam: «Ben kept an ace up his sleeve for the final round.» What does an ace up your sleeve mean? | A card he has lost | A dance step | *A secret advantage | A dirty sleeve
